{"cartConfigs":{"isActive":false},"dynamic_pages":[],"options":{"mobileOnly":false,"versionID":null},"page":[{"id":"sec_2101","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":72}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":66}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2102","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">DIJAE DADULA</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":16,"fontWeight":"800","height":24,"left":160,"letterSpacing":"3px","lineHeight":"1.4","top":26,"width":260}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"800","height":22,"left":20,"letterSpacing":"2px","lineHeight":"1.4","top":22}}}},{"id":"b_2103","type":"button","specials":{"text":"Subscribe"},"events":[{"action":"open_link","id":"ev_2104","target":"https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter","targetURL":"_self","type":"click"}],"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(0,122,102,1)","borderRadius":"8px","color":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"700","height":40,"left":650,"textAlign":"center","top":16}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(0,122,102,1)","borderRadius":"8px","color":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"700","height":38,"left":270,"textAlign":"center","top":14,"width":130}}}},{"id":"n_2105","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Newsletter</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":532,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"n_2106","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Blog</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":414,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"l_2107","type":"line","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":63,"width":960}},"mobile":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":60,"width":420}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2108","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":9123}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":11868}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2109","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Blog</a> · CRM and automation that sells"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":64,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":48,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2110","type":"text-block","specials":{"tag":"h1","text":"Automation for Coaches and Consultants: From Inquiry to Booked Call"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":42,"fontWeight":"800","height":154,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":105,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":30,"fontWeight":"800","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":84,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2111","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"A six-stage booking system that replies in minutes, qualifies with three questions, books and reminds, and follows up once, with copy-ready messages and a scorecard."},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":21,"fontWeight":"400","height":98,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":277,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":18,"fontWeight":"400","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":210,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2112","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"By <a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Dijae Dadula</a> · November 28, 2026 · 9 min read"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":393,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":336,"width":380}}}},{"id":"eb_2120","type":"editor-blog","specials":{"html":"<div class='dd-article'>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><div class='dd-shot' style='aspect-ratio:16/9'><img src='https://statics.pancake.vn/web-media-264/8a/40/f3/1b/ce28c5cc800b9d3930197335389dc35262839d24a5ed01c26cd38c8a-w:1536-h:864-l:30989-t:image/jpeg.jpg' alt='Dark flat illustration of a chat bubble, three progress dots and a dashed path leading to a calendar with one green checked day and a notification bell, no text' width='1536' height='864' loading='lazy'></div></figure>\n<p>Automation for coaches and consultants works best as one simple system: reply to every inquiry within minutes, ask three qualifying questions, send a booking link only to people who fit, remind them before the call, and follow up once if they go quiet. Every step can run on its own. You show up to calls with people who are ready to talk.</p>\n<p>Many coaching and consulting practices don't lose clients to a better competitor. They lose them in the gap between “I'm interested” and a booked call, while the coach is busy coaching. This guide shows how to close that gap step by step, whichever tools you use, with copy-ready messages and the numbers to watch. It is AI automation for coaches and consultants at its most practical: coaching business automation that books calls, not a stack of tools.</p>\n<div class='dd-tldr'>\n<p class='dd-tldr-title'>What you will get</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <b>six-stage booking system</b> from first message to booked call.</li>\n<li><b>Copy-ready messages</b>: first reply, qualifying questions, booking, reminders and a win-back.</li>\n<li>The <b>Messenger rules</b> that decide when you can follow up.</li>\n<li>A <b>scorecard</b> to check that the system works.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class='dd-toc'><p class='dd-toc-title'>On this page</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href='#leak'>Where coaches lose clients before the call</a></li>\n<li><a href='#system'>The six-stage booking system</a></li>\n<li><a href='#reply'>Reply in minutes on every channel</a></li>\n<li><a href='#qualify'>Qualify with three questions</a></li>\n<li><a href='#book'>Book, confirm and remind</a></li>\n<li><a href='#silence'>What if they don't show up or go quiet?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#crm'>Track it in your CRM</a></li>\n<li><a href='#human'>What automation for coaches should not do</a></li>\n<li><a href='#faq'>Frequently asked questions</a></li>\n</ol></div>\n<h2 id='leak'>1. Where coaches lose clients before the call</h2>\n<p>A solo coach or a small consulting firm usually has the same weak points, and none of them are about the offer:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Slow first reply.</b> Inquiries arrive in the evening, on weekends or during sessions. By the time someone answers, the person has moved on. The research on speed-to-lead is covered in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/lead-response-time'>Lead Response Time: Why the First Five Minutes Decide Who Wins the Customer</a>.</li>\n<li><b>Calendar back-and-forth.</b> “What time works for you?” turns into four messages and two days.</li>\n<li><b>Calls with the wrong people.</b> Without a few questions first, discovery calls fill up with people who can't buy, aren't ready or need a different service.</li>\n<li><b>No-shows and silence.</b> A booked call with no reminder is easy to forget, and a lead who stops replying is usually never contacted again.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each leak is small. Together they decide how many paying clients come out of the same number of inquiries.</p>\n<h2 id='system'>2. The six-stage booking system</h2>\n<p>Think of consultant booking automation as six stages, from inquiry to booked call. Each stage has one job and one rule for moving to the next.</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><svg class='dk' viewBox='0 0 640 300' role='img' aria-labelledby='ca1t ca1d'>\n<title id='ca1t'>Six stages from inquiry to booked call</title>\n<desc id='ca1d'>Six boxes in two rows connected by arrows: 1 Reply in minutes, 2 Qualify with three questions, 3 Send the booking link, 4 Confirm and remind, 5 Follow up once on silence, 6 Log the stage in the CRM. The booking link box is highlighted in green.</desc>\n<defs><linearGradient id='ca1g' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#1f2224'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#0a0b0c'/></linearGradient>\n<marker id='ca1a' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z' fill='#8a8f94'/></marker></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='300' rx='14' fill='url(#ca1g)'/>\n<text x='24' y='36' class='svg-k'>INQUIRY TO BOOKED CALL · SIX STAGES</text>\n<rect x='24' y='60' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='40' y='92' class='svg-t'>1. Reply</text><text x='40' y='116' class='svg-s'>within minutes, 24/7</text>\n<rect x='232' y='60' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='248' y='92' class='svg-t'>2. Qualify</text><text x='248' y='116' class='svg-s'>three short questions</text>\n<rect x='440' y='60' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#10302a' stroke='#3fbfa6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='456' y='92' class='svg-t'>3. Book</text><text x='456' y='116' class='svg-s'>link only if they fit</text>\n<rect x='440' y='180' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='456' y='212' class='svg-t'>4. Remind</text><text x='456' y='236' class='svg-s'>confirm + 2 reminders</text>\n<rect x='232' y='180' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='248' y='212' class='svg-t'>5. Win back</text><text x='248' y='236' class='svg-s'>one message on silence</text>\n<rect x='24' y='180' width='176' height='80' rx='10' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='40' y='212' class='svg-t'>6. Log</text><text x='40' y='236' class='svg-s'>CRM stage + owner</text>\n<line x1='200' y1='100' x2='228' y2='100' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ca1a)'/>\n<line x1='408' y1='100' x2='436' y2='100' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ca1a)'/>\n<line x1='528' y1='140' x2='528' y2='176' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ca1a)'/>\n<line x1='440' y1='220' x2='412' y2='220' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ca1a)'/>\n<line x1='232' y1='220' x2='204' y2='220' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2' marker-end='url(#ca1a)'/>\n</svg><figcaption><b>Figure 1.</b> One job per stage. The booking link comes after qualification, not before.</figcaption></figure>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Job</th><th>Moves on when</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>1. Reply</td><td>Acknowledge and ask what they need</td><td>The person answers</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2. Qualify</td><td>Goal, timing, budget range</td><td>All three answers fit your offer</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3. Book</td><td>Send your booking page</td><td>A call is booked</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4. Remind</td><td>Confirm and remind before the call</td><td>The call happens</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5. Win back</td><td>One helpful message after silence</td><td>They reply, or you close the loop</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6. Log</td><td>Record the stage, source and next step</td><td>Always, at every stage</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id='reply'>3. Reply in minutes on every channel</h2>\n<p>Inquiries reach coaches through Facebook Messenger, Instagram, website forms and email. The first reply should go out on the same channel within minutes, day or night, and it should do one thing: start the conversation.</p>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>Hi [first name], thanks for reaching out! I'm [name]'s assistant.\nTo point you to the right next step, can I ask you 3 quick questions?</code></pre></div>\n<p>On Messenger, timing has rules. Meta's standard messaging window lasts 24 hours after the person's last message for most user actions; after that, businesses can only send messages that fit approved message tags. Meta's Human Agent feature lets a real person reply within 7 days of the person's last message, for issues that can't be solved inside the standard window. For reference, check the documentation <a href='https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/messenger-platform/policy' rel='noopener'>here</a>.</p>\n<p>In practice: do the qualifying and booking inside the first 24 hours, while the conversation is open. That is the strongest reason to reply instantly.</p>\n<div class='dd-note'><span class='dd-note-label'>Dijae's rule</span><p>The first reply is not the place to sell. Its only job is to get a second message from the person.</p></div>\n<h2 id='qualify'>4. Qualify with three questions</h2>\n<p>Three questions are enough to decide whether a discovery call makes sense. Ask them one at a time, with buttons where the channel allows it.</p>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>1. What's the main result you want help with? [short list of your services]\n2. When do you want to start? [This month / In 1-3 months / Just exploring]\n3. Which investment range fits you right now? [your ranges]</code></pre></div>\n<p>Then route on the answers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Fits all three:</b> send the booking link (stage 3).</li>\n<li><b>Just exploring:</b> send one useful resource and invite them to your newsletter. Don't push a call.</li>\n<li><b>Wrong service or budget:</b> say so kindly and point them to a better option if you have one.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A deeper version of this, with tags and handoff rules, is in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/qualify-leads-messenger-automatically'>How to Qualify Leads in Messenger Automatically</a>.</p>\n<h2 id='book'>5. Book, confirm and remind</h2>\n<p>Send a booking page, not a list of times. Booking call automation starts here, and most calendar tools now cover the basics. Google Calendar's appointment schedules, for example, include a shareable booking page, buffer time between appointments, a maximum number of bookings per day, a scheduling window, booking form questions, and confirmation and reminder emails. Some of these features need an eligible Google Workspace or Google One subscription. For reference, check the documentation <a href='https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/10729749?hl=en' rel='noopener'>here</a>.</p>\n<p>Set it up once with these rules:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Buffer time</b> between calls, so sessions never run into each other.</li>\n<li><b>A daily cap</b> on discovery calls, so client work keeps its time.</li>\n<li><b>Two or three booking-form questions</b> that you didn't already ask in chat.</li>\n<li><b>A confirmation right away and two reminders</b>: one the day before and one shortly before the call.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>Reminder: we're talking [day] at [time] ([time zone]).\nHere's the link: [meeting link]\nNeed a different time? Reschedule here: [link]</code></pre></div>\n<p>Always include a reschedule link. It gives someone whose plans changed an easy way to move the call instead of skipping it. If your calendar tool doesn't let you edit its reminder text, send this one by Messenger or email instead. Reminder timing and channels are covered in detail in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/appointment-no-show-reminders'>Appointment No-Shows: Reminder Systems That Actually Work</a>.</p>\n<h2 id='silence'>6. What if they don't show up or go quiet?</h2>\n<p>Two situations need one calm, automatic message each.</p>\n<p><b>A no-show.</b> Send a short note within the hour with a fresh booking link. No guilt, no lecture.</p>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>Looks like today's time didn't work out, no problem.\nIf you'd still like to talk, pick a new time here: [link]</code></pre></div>\n<p><b>Silence after qualifying.</b> If someone answered your questions but never booked, send one helpful follow-up a few days later, then stop. On Messenger, remember that this falls outside the 24-hour window unless they wrote again, so email is often the better channel for it when you have their address.</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><svg class='dk' viewBox='0 0 640 230' role='img' aria-labelledby='ca2t ca2d'>\n<title id='ca2t'>Messenger timing for coaches</title>\n<desc id='ca2d'>A timeline from the person's last message. The first 24 hours are highlighted green: reply, qualify and book here. From 24 hours to 7 days a grey band says a human agent may reply. After 7 days, outside the window, use email or wait for them to write again.</desc>\n<defs><linearGradient id='ca2g' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#1f2224'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#0a0b0c'/></linearGradient></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='230' rx='14' fill='url(#ca2g)'/>\n<text x='24' y='36' class='svg-k'>MESSENGER TIMING · FROM THEIR LAST MESSAGE</text>\n<rect x='24' y='70' width='180' height='56' rx='8' fill='#10302a' stroke='#3fbfa6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='38' y='96' class='svg-t'>0 to 24 hours</text><text x='38' y='116' class='svg-s'>reply, qualify, book</text>\n<rect x='212' y='70' width='220' height='56' rx='8' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/><text x='226' y='96' class='svg-t'>Up to 7 days</text><text x='226' y='116' class='svg-s'>a person may reply (Human Agent)</text>\n<rect x='440' y='70' width='176' height='56' rx='8' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='6 5'/><text x='454' y='96' class='svg-t'>After that</text><text x='454' y='116' class='svg-s'>email, or wait for them</text>\n<line x1='24' y1='152' x2='616' y2='152' stroke='#2a2e31' stroke-width='2'/>\n<circle cx='24' cy='152' r='6' fill='#3fbfa6'/><text x='24' y='180' class='svg-s'>their last message</text>\n<text x='24' y='210' class='svg-s'>Source: Meta Messenger Platform policy and Human Agent feature reference.</text>\n</svg><figcaption><b>Figure 2.</b> Do the important work inside the first 24 hours, while the conversation is open.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id='crm'>7. Track it in your CRM</h2>\n<p>Every inquiry should land in one place with a stage, a source and a next step, even if your CRM is a simple spreadsheet. Good automation for consultants and coaches turns the six stages into pipeline stages: Replied, Qualified, Booked, Showed, then Won or Lost. <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/crm-pipeline-stages-service-business'>CRM Pipeline Stages for Service Businesses</a> covers the exit rule for each stage.</p>\n<p>Then watch four numbers each week. They tell you exactly which stage leaks.</p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>How to calculate it</th><th>What a drop tells you</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>First reply time</td><td>Time from inquiry to first reply</td><td>The reply step is broken or off</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Qualify rate</td><td>Qualified ÷ replied</td><td>Questions are confusing, or ads attract the wrong people</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Booking rate</td><td>Booked ÷ qualified</td><td>The booking step has friction</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Show rate</td><td>Showed ÷ booked</td><td>Reminders are missing or too early</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><b>How you will know it works (acceptance test before you go live)</b></p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Pass when</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Send a test inquiry on each channel at night</td><td>A first reply arrives within minutes on every channel</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Answer “just exploring”</td><td>You get a resource, not a booking push</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Answer as a good fit</td><td>The booking link arrives and the CRM shows “Qualified”</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Book a test call</td><td>Confirmation now, reminders at the right times, reschedule link works</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Miss the test call</td><td>One no-show message with a new link, then nothing more</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id='human'>8. What automation for coaches should not do</h2>\n<p>Coaching and consulting are trust businesses. Automate the logistics, not the relationship.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Automate:</b> first replies, qualifying questions, booking, confirmations, reminders, no-show messages, CRM updates.</li>\n<li><b>Keep personal:</b> the discovery call itself, proposals, pricing conversations, anything emotional or sensitive, and any message where someone is upset.</li>\n<li><b>Always offer a person:</b> make it easy to ask for you directly at any point in the chat.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class='dd-warn'><span class='dd-note-label'>Be transparent</span><p>Say when an assistant or automation is replying. People don't mind a fast assistant; they mind feeling deceived.</p></div>\n<p>An honest limitation: this system books more of the right calls, but it can't fix an unclear offer or a weak discovery call. If people book and don't buy, the next thing to improve is the call and the offer, not the automation.</p>\n<h2 id='faq'>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>What should coaches automate first?</h3>\n<p>Start with the first reply and the booking link. Those two steps remove the slowest part of the process, the wait and the calendar back-and-forth, and they work on every channel.</p>\n<h3>How do consultants automate booking calls without seeming impersonal?</h3>\n<p>Keep the messages short and written in your own voice, ask only questions you genuinely need, and say clearly that an assistant handles scheduling. Keep the call, proposal and pricing conversation personal.</p>\n<h3>Can I follow up on Messenger after 24 hours?</h3>\n<p>Only in limited cases. Meta's standard window is 24 hours after the person's last message for most actions; a human agent may reply within 7 days, and other messages must fit approved message tags. Use email for later follow-ups when you have the address.</p>\n<h3>Do I need an expensive CRM to do this?</h3>\n<p>No. You need one place where every inquiry has a stage, a source and a next step. A simple CRM or even a well-kept sheet works at first; move to a CRM when you have more inquiries than you can track by hand.</p>\n<div class='dd-cta'><b>Get one practical AI idea every week.</b> Join the free weekly newsletter: <a href='https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter' rel='noopener'>Subscribe</a>. Want this booking system set up for your practice? Book a free AI Automation Blueprint call: <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/book' rel='noopener'>www.dijaedadula.com/book</a>.</div>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ol class='dd-refs'>\n<li>Meta for Developers, “Messenger Platform and IG Messaging API policy.” Checked November 2026. <a href='https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/messenger-platform/policy' rel='noopener'>developers.facebook.com</a></li>\n<li>Meta for Developers, “Human Agent” feature reference. Checked November 2026. <a href='https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/development/features-reference/human-agent' rel='noopener'>developers.facebook.com</a></li>\n<li>Google Calendar Help, “Create an appointment schedule.” Checked November 2026. <a href='https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/10729749?hl=en' rel='noopener'>support.google.com</a></li>\n<li>Google Calendar Help, “Learn about appointment schedules in Google Calendar.” Checked November 2026. <a href='https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/11608416' rel='noopener'>support.google.com</a></li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2>\n<ul class='dd-more'>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/get-more-clients-with-ai'>How Consultants, Coaches and Freelancers Can Get More Clients With AI</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/automate-lead-follow-up'>How to Automate Lead Follow-Up With AI</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/lead-response-time'>Lead Response Time: Why the First Five Minutes Decide Who Wins the Customer</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog'>See all posts on the blog</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":8616,"left":160,"top":450,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":11431,"left":20,"top":388,"width":380}}}},{"id":"h_css2121","type":"html-box","specials":{"html":"&lt;style&gt;.dd-article ul{list-style:disc outside !important}.dd-article ol{list-style:decimal outside !important}.dd-article li{display:list-item !important}.dd-article ul ul{list-style:circle outside !important}&lt;/style&gt;"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":1,"left":160,"top":9113,"width":1}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":1,"left":20,"top":11858,"width":1}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2141","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(247,248,250,1)","height":402}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(247,248,250,1)","height":508}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2142","type":"text-blo